<title>USA: TABLE-PXRE Q2 and six month net income rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE-PXRE Q2 and six month net income rises.</headline>
<dateline>EDISON, N.J. 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>PXRE Corp</p>
<p>						 Second Quarter</p>
<p>					  As Reported    Pro Forma</p>
<p>				     1997   1996  Change  1996 Change</p>
<p> Net premiums written	 $18,838 $10,740  75%$ 18,341   3%</p>
<p> Earned premiums		24,383  17,099  43%  30,012 (19%)</p>
<p> Revenues			 33,256  22,465  48%  37,553 (11%)</p>
<p>Income before extraordinary loss</p>
<p>				     12,915   7,185  80%  10,100  28%</p>
<p> Net income			11,960   7,185  66%  10,100  18%</p>
<p>Per share, fully diluted:</p>
<p>Before extraordinary loss</p>
<p>					 0.92    0.81  14%    0.69  33%</p>
<p>     Net income		    0.86    0.81   6%    0.69  25%</p>
<p> Operating income		12,720   7,251  62%  10,214  15%</p>
<p>Operating income per share,</p>
<p>   fully diluted		   0.91    0.82  11%    0.70  30%</p>
<p>						  First Six Months</p>
<p>					 As Reported    Pro Forma</p>
<p>				   1997    1996  Change  1996  Change</p>
<p> Net premiums written	$54,840 $36,087  52%$ 64,505 (15%)</p>
<p> Earned premiums		46,683  36,520  28%  63,355 (26%)</p>
<p> Revenues			 64,986  48,194  35%  78,759 (17%)</p>
<p>Income before extraordinary loss</p>
<p>				    24,961  16,494  51%  24,753    1%</p>
<p> Net income		     22,372  16,494  36%  24,753 (10%)</p>
<p>Per share, fully diluted:</p>
<p>Before extraordinary loss</p>
<p>					1.77    1.86  (5%)   1.70    4%</p>
<p>     Net income		   1.59    1.86 (15%)   1.70  (6%)</p>
<p> Operating income	     25,052  16,608  35%  24,947 (10%)</p>
<p>Operating income per share,</p>
<p>     fully diluted		1.78    1.87  (5%)   1.71    4%</p>
<p>	     (dollars in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE: -- Company says during Q2 it recorded an extraordinary loss of $955,000 and in the first six months, an extraordinary loss of $2,589,000, net of tax, related to the premium paid on the repurchase of $16.7 million of the company's 9.75 percent senior notes and the associated write-off of the pro rata share of the unamortized debt issuance costs.</p>
